// Mangekyō (万華鏡 · "Kaleidoscope")
// The Sharingan's next stage. Where Sharingan reads the quarter's look back, Mangekyō reads the daily candles inside it:
// the higher-timeframe fair value gaps, volume imbalances and suspension blocks ICT grades from the daily chart.
// • Daily gaps from the last 20 / 40 / 60 trading days, or from this week and last week only (ICT trades inside last week's
//   FVG), the most local ones above and below price; the one price is in graded in octants across the chart, with prices.
// • When price trades inside one, the candles that made it are drawn right of price, PO3-style.
// • Anchored as ICT draws them: an FVG from its first candle, a suspension block from the suspended candle; bodies read as the
//   chart's SET setting (or the settlement, the last trade, or the wider of the two, as ICT toggles SET for the widest imbalance).
// • Inversion FVGs kept after a close beyond, and the wick CEs of the last daily swing candle, as on ICT's daily chart.
// • Daily candles from the chart, the front-month contract, the continuous 1! or the back-adjusted 1!.
// • The card: each gap's size, status, tested reach odds (by Friday and in 20 days) and hold odds, and the week's
//   premium and discount draw.
// Tested on NQ, ES, RTY daily 2010–26 and YM 2017–26 against the same candles with no gap; the numbers are in the tooltips.
// Fair value gap, volume imbalance, suspension block, consequent encroachment, octant grading and PO3 are taught by ICT
// (Michael J. Huddleston). Not affiliated with or endorsed by ICT. Quarterly look backs live in Sharingan, the week's own
// range in Getsuga, opening gaps (NWOG / NDOG) in OpenGaps and RTH gaps in Benihime.

// behind_chart = false: the card, gaps and labels draw in front of the candles (Pine v6 defaults overlay visuals to behind the chart)
indicator("Mangekyō", "Mangekyō", overlay = true, behind_chart = false, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 300, max_boxes_count = 120)

TZ  = "America/New_York"
DAY = 86400000

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ Inputs
gV = "View"
themeI = input.string("Auto", "Theme", options = ["Auto", "Dark", "Light"], group = gV, tooltip = "Auto follows the chart background.", display = display.none)
crdSzI = input.string("Small", "Card text", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = gV, display = display.none)
layI   = input.string("Desktop", "Layout", options = ["Desktop", "Mobile"], group = gV, tooltip = "Mobile folds the card to the nearest gap above and below, the week and today.", display = display.none)
crdPos = input.string("Bottom left", "Card position", options = ["Top left", "Top center", "Top right", "Middle left", "Middle right", "Bottom left", "Bottom center", "Bottom right"], group = gV, display = display.none)

gD = "Daily data"
srcI = input.string("Chart symbol", "Daily candles from", options = ["Chart symbol", "Front-month contract", "Continuous 1!", "Continuous 1!, back-adjusted"], group = gD, tooltip = "Chart symbol: the daily candles of what is on the chart, with its own settings.\nFront-month contract: e.g. NQZ2026, as ICT charts it. Before the roll its candles were the deferred month's: thin (NQ 2010–24: 0.1% of the front month's volume 20–40 days out). Over the 60 days before each contract became front, its own chart showed every gap the front month showed plus 18% more on NQ, 5% ES, 93% RTY, 12% YM.\nContinuous 1!: unadjusted, it jumps at each roll by the carry. In 2022–26 the jump was 0.44–0.69 ATR (median; NQ 0.58), more than a typical daily gap is wide (0.28 ATR), so gaps from before the last roll sit at the old contract's prices.\nContinuous 1!, back-adjusted: the front month's candles with the roll jumps removed, so old gaps sit at today's contract prices. On an unadjusted chart the left end of an old gap will not line up with its candles.", display = display.none)
setI = input.string("As the chart (SET setting)", "Body close", options = ["As the chart (SET setting)", "Widest of the two (ICT)", "Settlement (SET on)", "Last trade (SET off)"], group = gD, tooltip = "A daily body ends at the settlement (TradingView's 'Use settlement as close on daily interval', SET) or at the last trade at 17:00 ET. Wicks are the same either way, so wick gaps (FVGs) do not change; volume imbalances and suspension blocks do.\nAs the chart: the bodies your chart shows, so every zone lines up with the candles.\nWidest of the two: each imbalance is read with whichever setting makes it wider, as ICT toggles SET to find the widest; a zone read with the other close is drawn with a dashed border, since it will not line up with the bodies on screen.\nTested 2018–26: last trade and settlement differ by 0.04 ATR on a typical day and by more than 0.1 ATR on 12–18% of days; the candle's colour flips on 3–5%. SET on gives 5–21% more volume imbalances and 10–57% more suspension blocks; only 44–50% of imbalances exist under both. Neither setting's imbalances held more often than the same candles without one.", display = display.none)

gG = "Gaps"
scI    = input.string("Look back (20 / 40 / 60 days)", "Gaps from", options = ["Look back (20 / 40 / 60 days)", "This week + last week", "Last week", "This week"], group = gG, tooltip = "Look back: every gap from the last 20, 40 or 60 trading days, the IPDA look backs.\nThe week settings keep only the gaps formed this week (today's forming FVG included) and / or last week, as ICT trades inside the previous week's FVG with its octants. A gap belongs to the week its last candle closed in. If price is in none of them, the nearest one is graded.", display = display.none)
lbI    = input.string("60", "Look back (trading days)", options = ["20", "40", "60"], group = gG, tooltip = "Gaps formed in the last 20, 40 or 60 trading days, the IPDA look backs (Sharingan draws the quarter itself).", active = scI == "Look back (20 / 40 / 60 days)", display = display.none)
nEach  = input.int(2, "Most local, each side", minval = 1, maxval = 8, group = gG, tooltip = "The nearest live gaps above and below price. Gaps price is inside are always drawn.", display = display.none)
useF   = input.bool(true, "FVG", group = gG, inline = "k1", display = display.none)
minF   = input.float(0.25, "≥ ATR", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gG, inline = "k1", tooltip = "Three candles whose wicks leave a gap: BISI (bullish, candle 3's low above candle 1's high) or SIBI (bearish). Width in daily ATR(14) at formation.\n2010–26, four markets: 54–60 a year per market, median 0.28 ATR; 70% are back within 5 days, 84% within 20.", active = useF, display = display.none)
dispF  = input.float(0.5, "Displacement: candle 2 body ≥ ATR", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = gG, tooltip = "Keeps the FVGs whose middle candle moved this far in the gap's direction. A filter for the major ones, not an edge: at the same width, displacement did not change how often a gap held.", active = useF, display = display.none)
useS   = input.bool(true, "Suspension block", group = gG, inline = "k2", display = display.none)
minS   = input.float(0.25, "≥ ATR", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gG, inline = "k2", tooltip = "A candle with a volume imbalance on both sides, as ICT defines it: the zone runs from the body before to the body after. 15–21 a year per market, median 0.55 ATR.", active = useS, display = display.none)
useVI  = input.bool(true, "Volume imbalance", group = gG, inline = "k3", display = display.none)
minVI  = input.float(0.10, "≥ ATR", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = gG, inline = "k3", tooltip = "Two candles whose bodies do not meet. 66–73 a year per market, median 0.05 ATR, so the size filter matters.", active = useVI, display = display.none)
showInv = input.bool(true, "Inversion FVGs", group = gG, tooltip = "An FVG closed beyond on the daily chart flips: ICT trades it as an inversion FVG from the other side. Kept, in their own colour, through the look back, until a daily close beyond its other edge. Suspension blocks and imbalances end at a close beyond.\nTested: inverted FVGs were retested within 20 days 88.5% of the time vs 89.6% for the same candles without a gap, held the touch day 43.5% vs 44.4%, and 10 days 25.8% vs 24.4%: drawn, not scored.", display = display.none)
mergeOv = input.bool(true, "Merge overlapping gaps", group = gG, tooltip = "Where two drawn gaps on the same side (support or resistance) overlap by half or more of the smaller one, one is drawn: a live gap before an inversion FVG, an FVG before a suspension block before an imbalance, else the wider.", display = display.none)
hideDef = input.bool(true, "Hide gaps from the deferred month", group = gG, tooltip = "Front-month contract only: gaps whose middle candle traded under 10% of the contract's recent daily volume, i.e. before it became the front month.", active = srcI == "Front-month contract", display = display.none)

gR = "Drawing"
gradeI = input.string("CE", "Grade", options = ["CE", "Quadrants", "Octants"], group = gR, tooltip = "Lines across every drawn gap. The gap price is inside is always graded in octants with prices.\nTested: the touch day's wick stopped across the zone about as a same-size band without a gap does; within 1/16 of CE 12.5% vs 11.3%.", display = display.none)
extB   = input.int(0, "Extend right (bars, 0 = auto)", minval = 0, maxval = 400, group = gR, tooltip = "How far past the last bar the gaps and their grades run, labels at the end. Auto: 14 bars on a daily chart; intraday 110 (1–2 minute), 70 (3–5 minute), 40 (longer), so they run past the PO3 candles.", display = display.none)
wickI  = input.string("Last daily swing", "Daily wick CE", options = ["Last daily swing", "Yesterday", "Off"], group = gR, tooltip = "The midpoint of a daily candle's premium wick (high to the body top), of its discount wick (body bottom to the low) and the midpoint between the two, run right, as ICT grades the wicks of the day that turned price.\nLast daily swing: the newest daily high or low with a higher (lower) candle on each side; or yesterday, while it is a pending swing: a lower low (higher high) than the day before that today has not traded past, as ICT grades Friday's candle over the weekend. Yesterday: the last completed day.\nICT's reading, drawn; not tested here.", display = display.none)
cWick  = input.color(#7e57c2, "Wick CE", group = gR, inline = "c3", active = wickI != "Off", display = display.none)
cCE    = input.color(#089981, "CE of the graded gap", group = gR, inline = "c4", tooltip = "The gap price is in (or, with a week setting, the nearest one) is graded across the chart in solid lines at every eighth, its CE in this colour, prices at the right end, as ICT grades it on the 1-minute chart.", display = display.none)
cBull  = input.color(#26a69a, "BISI", group = gR, inline = "c1", display = display.none)
cBear  = input.color(#ef5350, "SIBI", group = gR, inline = "c1", display = display.none)
cSBc   = input.color(#42a5f5, "Suspension", group = gR, inline = "c2", display = display.none)
cVIc   = input.color(#9575cd, "Imbalance", group = gR, inline = "c2", display = display.none)
cInv   = input.color(#ff9800, "Inversion FVG", group = gR, inline = "c3", active = showInv, display = display.none)
boxTr  = input.int(84, "Fill transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gR, display = display.none)

gP = "PO3 · the gap's candles right of price"
po3I   = input.string("When price is inside a gap", "Show", options = ["When price is inside a gap", "Always (nearest gap)", "Off"], group = gP, tooltip = "The two or three daily candles that made the gap, drawn right of price with the gap shaded and graded, and where price is now.", display = display.none)
pOff   = input.int(0, "Offset from chart (bars, 0 = auto)", minval = 0, maxval = 400, group = gP, tooltip = "Auto: 3 bars on a daily chart; intraday 25 (1–2 minute), 15 (3–5 minute), 10 (longer).", active = po3I != "Off", display = display.none)
pW     = input.int(0, "Candle width (bars, 0 = auto)", minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = gP, tooltip = "Auto: 2 bars on a daily chart; intraday 16 (1–2 minute), 10 (3–5 minute), 5 (longer).", active = po3I != "Off", display = display.none)
pSp    = input.int(0, "Spacing (0 = auto)", minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = gP, tooltip = "Auto: 1 bar on a daily chart; intraday 8 (1–2 minute), 5 (3–5 minute), 3 (longer).", active = po3I != "Off", display = display.none)
pCol   = input.color(#787b86, "Candle colour", group = gP, active = po3I != "Off", display = display.none)

gC = "Card"
showCrd = input.bool(true, "Card", group = gC, display = display.none)
showP   = input.bool(true, "Tested odds", group = gC, tooltip = "Reach: the chance the gap's near edge trades by Friday and within 20 trading days, from its distance at the last close in daily ATR(14). Fit on NQ, ES, RTY, YM daily 2010–26 on the nearest live gap above and below. Walk-forward 2014–26 (each year fit on the years before), 5 days: above 6→5%, 21→22%, 41→36%, 60→57%, 81→79%, 95→94%; below 6→10%, 21→22%, 40→41%, 60→61%, 80→82%, 95→95%. Single years ran 0.85–1.20× the average.\nHolds: the chance the first touch day does not trade through the far edge, then that it is not closed beyond within 10 trading days, from the gap's width. FVG: 0.25 ATR wide 48% · 29%, 0.5 ATR 71% · 35%, 1 ATR 87% · 42%. Locked test 2025–26 (fit on 2010–24), touch day: 11→14%, 37→41%, 59→57%, 79→82%.", active = showCrd, display = display.none)

gN = "Alerts (create one alert with 'Any alert() function call')"
alIn = input.bool(true, "Price enters a gap", group = gN, inline = "a1", display = display.none)
alCE = input.bool(true, "CE traded", group = gN, inline = "a1", display = display.none)
alX  = input.bool(true, "Closed beyond", group = gN, inline = "a2", display = display.none)
alNw = input.bool(false, "New gap", group = gN, inline = "a2", display = display.none)

int  LB  = str.tonumber(lbI) == 20 ? 20 : str.tonumber(lbI) == 40 ? 40 : 60
int  scM = scI == "This week + last week" ? 1 : scI == "Last week" ? 2 : scI == "This week" ? 3 : 0
bool mob = layI == "Mobile"
int  setM = setI == "Settlement (SET on)" ? 0 : setI == "Last trade (SET off)" ? 1 : setI == "Widest of the two (ICT)" ? 2 : 3
bool isD  = timeframe.isdaily
// auto sizes by timeframe: a 1-minute chart shows ~600–1,200 bars, so the PO3 candles and the run past price scale with it
int  tfS  = timeframe.in_seconds()
int  tfK  = isD ? 0 : tfS <= 120 ? 3 : tfS <= 300 ? 2 : 1
int  xB   = extB > 0 ? extB : tfK == 0 ? 14 : tfK == 3 ? 110 : tfK == 2 ? 70 : 40
int  pO   = pOff > 0 ? pOff : tfK == 0 ? 3 : tfK == 3 ? 25 : tfK == 2 ? 15 : 10
int  pWd  = pW > 0 ? pW : tfK == 0 ? 2 : tfK == 3 ? 16 : tfK == 2 ? 10 : 5
int  pS   = pSp > 0 ? pSp : tfK == 0 ? 1 : tfK == 3 ? 8 : tfK == 2 ? 5 : 3

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ Palette, helpers
float bgLum = 0.299 * color.r(chart.bg_color) + 0.587 * color.g(chart.bg_color) + 0.114 * color.b(chart.bg_color)
bool  dark  = themeI == "Dark" or (themeI == "Auto" and bgLum < 128)
color cBg   = dark ? #0e1117 : #ffffff
color cHd   = dark ? #171c28 : #eef1f6
color cBd   = dark ? #262c3a : #d5dae4
color cTx   = dark ? #e6e9ef : #131722
color cSub  = dark ? #9aa3b5 : #4a5163
color cMu   = dark ? #5d6476 : #9aa1b2
crdSz = crdSzI == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : crdSzI == "Small" ? size.small : size.normal
posOf(string s) =>
    switch s
        "Top left"      => position.top_left
        "Top center"    => position.top_center
        "Top right"     => position.top_right
        "Middle left"   => position.middle_left
        "Middle right"  => position.middle_right
        "Bottom left"   => position.bottom_left
        "Bottom center" => position.bottom_center
        => position.bottom_right
dmy(int t) => str.format_time(t + 6 * 3600000, "dd MMM", TZ)
decOf(float m) =>
    int nd = 8
    for k = 0 to 8
        float x = m * math.pow(10, k)
        if math.abs(x - math.round(x)) < 1e-7
            nd := k
            break
    nd
var int    ND  = decOf(syminfo.mintick)
var string PXF = "#,##0" + (ND > 0 ? "." + str.repeat("0", ND) : "")
px(float v) => str.tostring(v, PXF)
pc0(float p) => str.tostring(p * 100.0, "0") + "%"
f2(float v) => str.tostring(v, "0.00")
nCdf(float x) =>
    float z = math.abs(x)
    float t = 1.0 / (1.0 + 0.2316419 * z)
    float p = 1.0 - 0.3989422804 * math.exp(-0.5 * z * z) * t * (0.319381530 + t * (-0.356563782 + t * (1.781477937 + t * (-1.821255978 + t * 1.330274429))))
    x >= 0 ? p : 1.0 - p
lgs(float z) => 1.0 / (1.0 + math.exp(-z))
// tested reach odds: p = logistic(a + b·logit(2Φ(−d / (κ·√h)))), d = distance in ATR(14) at the last close, h = trading days
reachP(float d, float h, bool above) =>
    float k = above ? 0.625 : 1.05
    float a = above ? 0.2108 : -1.0257
    float b = above ? 0.9973 : 1.0638
    float q = math.min(math.max(2.0 * nCdf(-(d / math.sqrt(math.max(h, 0.25))) / k), 0.00001), 0.99999)
    lgs(a + b * math.log(q / (1.0 - q)))
// tested hold odds from the width w (ATR): the first touch day does not trade through the far edge · not closed beyond within 10 days
pTouch(int kind, float w) =>
    float lw = math.log(math.max(w, 0.01))
    kind == 0 ? lgs(1.9063 + 1.4383 * lw) : kind == 1 ? lgs(1.8216 + 1.5525 * lw) : lgs(1.1063 + 1.0892 * lw)
p10(int kind, float w) =>
    float lw = math.log(math.max(w, 0.01))
    kind == 0 ? lgs(-0.3164 + 0.4153 * lw) : kind == 1 ? lgs(-0.0963 + 0.6071 * lw) : lgs(-0.8334 + 0.2189 * lw)
// survives the next 10 trading days after the touch day, by where the touch day closed: back outside · near half · far half
pBody(int kind, int zoneHalf) =>
    kind == 0 ? (zoneHalf == 0 ? 0.439 : zoneHalf == 1 ? 0.342 : 0.161) : kind == 1 ? (zoneHalf == 0 ? 0.508 : zoneHalf == 1 ? 0.448 : 0.198) : (zoneHalf == 0 ? 0.324 : zoneHalf == 1 ? 0.241 : 0.159)

// CME equity-index holidays (as Kyōka Suigetsu / Sharingan), for counting the trading days left this week
dowOf(int y, int m, int d) => dayofweek(timestamp("UTC", y, m, d, 0, 0), "UTC")
nthDow(int y, int m, int wd, int n) =>
    int f = dowOf(y, m, 1)
    1 + (wd - f + 7) % 7 + 7 * (n - 1)
lastDow(int y, int m, int wd, int dim) =>
    int ld = dowOf(y, m, dim)
    dim - (ld - wd + 7) % 7
easterTs(int y) =>
    int a  = y % 19
    int b  = int(math.floor(y / 100.0))
    int c  = y % 100
    int d  = int(math.floor(b / 4.0))
    int e  = b % 4
    int f  = int(math.floor((b + 8) / 25.0))
    int g  = int(math.floor((b - f + 1) / 3.0))
    int h  = (19 * a + b - d - g + 15) % 30
    int i  = int(math.floor(c / 4.0))
    int k  = c % 4
    int lw = (32 + 2 * e + 2 * i - h - k) % 7
    int mm = int(math.floor((a + 11 * h + 22 * lw) / 451.0))
    int mo = int(math.floor((h + lw - 7 * mm + 114) / 31.0))
    int dd = (h + lw - 7 * mm + 114) % 31 + 1
    timestamp("UTC", y, mo, dd, 0, 0)
isHol(int y, int m, int d) =>
    int  w   = dowOf(y, m, d)
    bool hol = false
    if w >= 2 and w <= 6
        int  gf     = easterTs(y) - 2 * DAY
        bool gfOpen = y == 2010 or y == 2012 or y == 2015 or y == 2023 or y == 2026
        hol := (m == 1 and (d == 1 or (d == 2 and w == 2))) or (m == 1 and d == nthDow(y, 1, 2, 3)) or (m == 2 and d == nthDow(y, 2, 2, 3)) or (not gfOpen and m == month(gf, "UTC") and d == dayofmonth(gf, "UTC")) or (m == 5 and d == lastDow(y, 5, 2, 31)) or (y >= 2022 and m == 6 and (d == 19 or (d == 18 and w == 6) or (d == 20 and w == 2))) or (m == 7 and (d == 4 or (d == 3 and w == 6) or (d == 5 and w == 2))) or (m == 9 and d == nthDow(y, 9, 2, 1)) or (m == 11 and d == nthDow(y, 11, 5, 4)) or (m == 12 and (d == 25 or (d == 24 and w == 6) or (d == 26 and w == 2)))
    hol
// trading days from today (a trading date at UTC midnight) through Friday, today included
daysToFri(int td) =>
    int n = 0
    int t = td
    while dayofweek(t, "UTC") != dayofweek.saturday
        if dayofweek(t, "UTC") != dayofweek.sunday and not isHol(year(t, "UTC"), month(t, "UTC"), dayofmonth(t, "UTC"))
            n += 1
        t += DAY
    math.max(n, 1)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ The daily data
bool isFut  = syminfo.type == "futures"
bool isCont = str.contains(syminfo.ticker, "!")
string cont = isFut and syminfo.root != "" ? syminfo.prefix + ":" + syminfo.root + "1!" : syminfo.tickerid
string base = switch srcI
    "Front-month contract"         => isFut and isCont and not na(syminfo.current_contract) and syminfo.current_contract != "" ? syminfo.current_contract : syminfo.tickerid
    "Continuous 1!"                => cont
    "Continuous 1!, back-adjusted" => cont
    => syminfo.tickerid
string tkS = srcI == "Continuous 1!, back-adjusted" ? ticker.modify(base, backadjustment = backadjustment.on, settlement_as_close = settlement_as_close.on) : srcI == "Continuous 1!" ? ticker.modify(base, backadjustment = backadjustment.off, settlement_as_close = settlement_as_close.on) : ticker.modify(base, settlement_as_close = settlement_as_close.on)
string tkL = srcI == "Continuous 1!, back-adjusted" ? ticker.modify(base, backadjustment = backadjustment.on, settlement_as_close = settlement_as_close.off) : srcI == "Continuous 1!" ? ticker.modify(base, backadjustment = backadjustment.off, settlement_as_close = settlement_as_close.off) : ticker.modify(base, settlement_as_close = settlement_as_close.off)
string tkC = srcI == "Continuous 1!, back-adjusted" ? ticker.modify(base, backadjustment = backadjustment.on, settlement_as_close = settlement_as_close.inherit) : srcI == "Continuous 1!" ? ticker.modify(base, backadjustment = backadjustment.off, settlement_as_close = settlement_as_close.inherit) : ticker.modify(base, settlement_as_close = settlement_as_close.inherit)
// the main read: the chart's setting, settlement or last trade; Widest adds the last-trade read to the settlement read
string tkA = setM == 3 ? tkC : setM == 1 ? tkL : tkS

type Gap
    int   t1           // time of the first candle (daily bar time = its 18:00 ET session start)
    int   t2           // time of the middle candle (the second of two for an imbalance)
    int   t0           // time of the last candle, the day it formed
    int   kind         // 0 FVG · 1 suspension block · 2 volume imbalance
    int   dir          // 1 bullish (BISI), -1 bearish (SIBI)
    float top
    float bot
    float atr          // ATR(14) at formation
    float disp         // the middle candle's body in ATR, in the gap's direction
    float rv           // the middle candle's volume / the 20 days before
    float v2           // the middle candle's volume
    bool  brk          // the move closed beyond the last swing (3 bars each side) in its direction
    int   age = 0      // trading days since it formed
    int   tT           // first touch of the near edge
    int   tM           // CE traded
    int   tF           // far edge traded (wick through)
    int   tX           // closed beyond the far edge (an FVG then becomes an inversion FVG)
    int   tY           // an inversion FVG closed beyond its other edge: it is spent
    float dp           // deepest penetration so far, 0 = near edge, 1 = far edge
    int   src = 0      // 0 settlement close, 1 last trade
    int   nc = 3       // candles that made it
    float o1
    float h1
    float l1
    float c1
    float o2
    float h2
    float l2
    float c2
    float o3
    float h3
    float l3
    float c3

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ Daily engine (runs on the daily series)
// Completed days only ([1] and older), so it reads the same on any chart timeframe and never repaints.
// A gap is a copy of this bar's candle template (three candles [3] [2] [1], or two [2] [1] for an imbalance) with its zone set.
// Candle 2 in the template is the middle candle (FVG, suspension block) or the gapping candle (imbalance).
addGap(array<Gap> gs, Gap tpl, int kind, int dir, float top, float bot, float rv, bool brk, int srcId) =>
    Gap g = tpl.copy()
    g.kind := kind
    g.dir  := dir
    g.top  := top
    g.bot  := bot
    g.rv   := rv
    g.brk  := brk
    g.src  := srcId
    g.disp := (g.c2 - g.o2) * dir / g.atr
    gs.push(g)
engine(int srcId) =>
    var array<Gap> gs = array.new<Gap>()
    var float shP = na
    var float slP = na
    float a1   = ta.atr(14)[1]
    float vAvg = ta.sma(volume, 20)
    float hh7  = ta.highest(high, 7)[1]
    float ll7  = ta.lowest(low, 7)[1]
    Gap   T3   = Gap.new(t1 = time[3], t2 = time[2], t0 = time[1], atr = a1, v2 = volume[2], nc = 3, o1 = open[3], h1 = high[3], l1 = low[3], c1 = close[3], o2 = open[2], h2 = high[2], l2 = low[2], c2 = close[2], o3 = open[1], h3 = high[1], l3 = low[1], c3 = close[1])
    Gap   T2   = Gap.new(t1 = time[2], t2 = time[1], t0 = time[1], atr = a1, v2 = volume[1], nc = 2, o1 = open[2], h1 = high[2], l1 = low[2], c1 = close[2], o2 = open[1], h2 = high[1], l2 = low[1], c2 = close[1])
    // swings: the extreme of 7 completed bars, centre 4 bars back
    if bar_index > 8
        if high[4] == hh7
            shP := high[4]
        if low[4] == ll7
            slP := low[4]
    if bar_index > 25 and not na(a1) and a1 > 0
        // 1. drop what has left the longest look back, and gaps closed beyond before the newest completed day
        if gs.size() > 0
            for i = gs.size() - 1 to 0
                Gap g = gs.get(i)
                if g.age >= 60 or (not na(g.tX) and (g.kind != 0 or not showInv)) or not na(g.tY)
                    gs.remove(i)
        // 2. the newest completed day against every gap formed before it
        for g in gs
            g.age += 1
            if na(g.tX)
                float w = g.top - g.bot
                if g.dir == 1
                    if na(g.tT) and low[1] <= g.top
                        g.tT := time[1]
                    if na(g.tM) and low[1] <= (g.top + g.bot) / 2.0
                        g.tM := time[1]
                    if na(g.tF) and low[1] <= g.bot
                        g.tF := time[1]
                    if not na(g.tT) and w > 0
                        g.dp := math.max(nz(g.dp, 0.0), (g.top - low[1]) / w)
                    if close[1] < g.bot
                        g.tX := time[1]
                else
                    if na(g.tT) and high[1] >= g.bot
                        g.tT := time[1]
                    if na(g.tM) and high[1] >= (g.top + g.bot) / 2.0
                        g.tM := time[1]
                    if na(g.tF) and high[1] >= g.top
                        g.tF := time[1]
                    if not na(g.tT) and w > 0
                        g.dp := math.max(nz(g.dp, 0.0), (high[1] - g.bot) / w)
                    if close[1] > g.top
                        g.tX := time[1]
            else if na(g.tY) and ((g.dir == 1 and close[1] > g.top) or (g.dir == -1 and close[1] < g.bot))
                g.tY := time[1]
        // 3. new gaps formed by the newest completed day
        float bt1 = math.max(open[1], close[1])
        float bb1 = math.min(open[1], close[1])
        float bt2 = math.max(open[2], close[2])
        float bb2 = math.min(open[2], close[2])
        float bt3 = math.max(open[3], close[3])
        float bb3 = math.min(open[3], close[3])
        float rv2 = nz(vAvg[3]) > 0 ? volume[2] / vAvg[3] : na
        float rv1 = nz(vAvg[2]) > 0 ? volume[1] / vAvg[2] : na
        bool  brU = not na(shP) and math.max(close[1], close[2]) > shP
        bool  brD = not na(slP) and math.min(close[1], close[2]) < slP
        if useF
            if low[1] > high[3] and (low[1] - high[3]) / a1 >= minF and (close[2] - open[2]) / a1 >= dispF
                addGap(gs, T3, 0, 1, low[1], high[3], rv2, brU, srcId)
            else if high[1] < low[3] and (low[3] - high[1]) / a1 >= minF and (open[2] - close[2]) / a1 >= dispF
                addGap(gs, T3, 0, -1, low[3], high[1], rv2, brD, srcId)
        // suspension block: a volume imbalance on both sides of the middle candle
        if useS
            if bb1 > bt2 and bb2 > bt3 and (bb1 - bt3) / a1 >= minS
                addGap(gs, T3, 1, 1, bb1, bt3, rv2, brU, srcId)
            else if bt1 < bb2 and bt2 < bb3 and (bb3 - bt1) / a1 >= minS
                addGap(gs, T3, 1, -1, bb3, bt1, rv2, brD, srcId)
        // volume imbalance: the newest two bodies do not meet
        if useVI
            if bb1 > bt2 and (bb1 - bt2) / a1 >= minVI
                addGap(gs, T2, 2, 1, bb1, bt2, rv1, brU, srcId)
            else if bt1 < bb2 and (bb2 - bt1) / a1 >= minVI
                addGap(gs, T2, 2, -1, bb2, bt1, rv1, brD, srcId)
        while gs.size() > 60
            gs.shift()
    gs

// the last daily swing candle (a lower low, or higher high, than the completed candle on each side) and yesterday, for the wick CEs
swingDay() =>
    var float sO = na
    var float sH = na
    var float sL = na
    var float sC = na
    var int   sT = na
    var int   sD = 0
    if bar_index > 3
        bool swL = low[2] < low[1] and low[2] < low[3]
        bool swH = high[2] > high[1] and high[2] > high[3]
        if swL or swH
            sO := open[2]
            sH := high[2]
            sL := low[2]
            sC := close[2]
            sT := time[2]
            sD := swL and swH ? 0 : swL ? 1 : -1
    // yesterday as a pending swing: a lower low (higher high) than the day before, not yet confirmed by today
    int pD = low[1] < low[2] and not (high[1] > high[2]) ? 1 : high[1] > high[2] and not (low[1] < low[2]) ? -1 : 0
    [sO, sH, sL, sC, sT, sD, pD]
array<Gap> gS = request.security(tkA, "D", engine(0), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on, calc_bars_count = 600)
array<Gap> gL = request.security(tkL, "D", engine(1), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on, calc_bars_count = 600)
[atr, lastC, vMed, lastT, lastO, pH2, pL2, pT2, yH, yL] = request.security(tkA, "D", [ta.atr(14)[1], close[1], ta.median(volume, 20)[1], time[1], open[1], high[2], low[2], time[2], high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on, calc_bars_count = 600)
[wsO, wsH, wsL, wsC, wsT, wsD, wpD] = request.security(tkA, "D", swingDay(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on, calc_bars_count = 600)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ Today, on the chart
bool tfOK = timeframe.isintraday or timeframe.isdaily
var float tdH = na
var float tdL = na
var float tdO = na
bool newTD = time_tradingday != time_tradingday[1]
if newTD
    tdO := open
    tdH := high
    tdL := low
else
    tdH := math.max(tdH, high)
    tdL := math.min(tdL, low)

// the gaps on show: the main read, plus (Widest) the last-trade read where it gives the wider imbalance
same(Gap a, Gap b) => a.t0 == b.t0 and a.dir == b.dir and a.kind == b.kind
pick() =>
    array<Gap> out = array.new<Gap>()
    if not na(gS)
        for g in gS
            out.push(g)
    if setM == 2 and not na(gL)
        for g in gL
            if g.kind != 0
                int at = -1
                if out.size() > 0
                    for i = 0 to out.size() - 1
                        if same(out.get(i), g)
                            at := i
                            break
                if at < 0
                    out.push(g)
                else if g.top - g.bot > out.get(at).top - out.get(at).bot
                    out.set(at, g)
    out

// an FVG closed beyond on the daily chart is an inversion FVG; its role flips (support ↔ resistance)
inv(Gap g) => not na(g.tX)
role(Gap g) => inv(g) ? -g.dir : g.dir
// ICT names a gap by its displacement candle: the middle candle (the gapping candle of an imbalance)
dayNm(int t) => str.format_time(t + 6 * 3600000, "EEE dd MMM", TZ)
baseNm(Gap g) => g.kind == 0 ? (g.dir == 1 ? "▲ BISI" : "▼ SIBI") : g.kind == 1 ? (g.dir == 1 ? "▲ SB" : "▼ SB") : (g.dir == 1 ? "▲ VI" : "▼ VI")
kindNm(Gap g) => inv(g) ? (g.dir == 1 ? "▼ IFVG" : "▲ IFVG") : baseNm(g)
colOf(Gap g) => inv(g) ? cInv : g.kind == 1 ? cSBc : g.kind == 2 ? cVIc : g.dir == 1 ? cBull : cBear
// where ICT draws it from: an FVG and an imbalance from their first candle, a suspension block from the suspended candle
anchorT(Gap g) => g.kind == 1 ? g.t2 : g.t1
bool defMode = srcI == "Front-month contract"
isDef(Gap g) => defMode and not na(vMed) and vMed > 0 and not na(g.v2) and g.v2 < 0.10 * vMed
// has today's range reached the gap's near edge (the side price comes from)?
todayIn(Gap g) => role(g) == 1 ? tdL <= g.top : tdH >= g.bot
nearEdge(Gap g) => role(g) == 1 ? g.top : g.bot
// where a price sits in the gap: 0 = near edge, 1 = far edge
inZ(Gap g, float p) => g.top > g.bot ? (role(g) == 1 ? (g.top - p) / (g.top - g.bot) : (p - g.bot) / (g.top - g.bot)) : na
insideNow(Gap g) => close <= g.top and close >= g.bot
statusOf(Gap g) =>
    string s = ""
    float dpT = todayIn(g) ? inZ(g, role(g) == 1 ? tdL : tdH) : na
    float dpA = math.max(nz(g.dp, -1.0), nz(dpT, -1.0))
    bool  tch = not na(g.tT) or todayIn(g)
    if inv(g)
        s := "inverted " + dmy(g.tX) + (insideNow(g) ? " · inside now" : "")
    else if insideNow(g)
        s := "inside now"
    else if not tch
        s := "untouched"
    else if dpA >= 1.0
        s := "traded through" + (na(g.tT) ? " today" : "")
    else if dpA >= 0.5
        s := "past CE" + (na(g.tT) ? " today" : "")
    else
        s := (na(g.tT) ? "touched today" : "touched " + dmy(g.tT))
    s

// the FVG today's candle is forming (candle 1 = the day before yesterday, candle 2 = yesterday); the engine takes it in at the
// next session's open, once the day is complete, so over a weekend Friday's gap shows here as formed
int   fmDir = 0
float fmTop = na
float fmBot = na
if useF and not na(atr) and atr > 0 and not na(pH2)
    if tdL > pH2 and (tdL - pH2) / atr >= minF and (lastC - lastO) / atr >= dispF
        fmDir := 1
        fmTop := tdL
        fmBot := pH2
    else if tdH < pL2 and (pL2 - tdH) / atr >= minF and (lastO - lastC) / atr >= dispF
        fmDir := -1
        fmTop := pL2
        fmBot := tdH

int  dayNow = time_tradingday
int  dLeft  = daysToFri(timestamp("UTC", year(dayNow, "UTC"), month(dayNow, "UTC"), dayofmonth(dayNow, "UTC"), 0, 0))
// this week's Monday (UTC midnight): a gap touched before it is not this week's draw
int  wkStart = timestamp("UTC", year(dayNow, "UTC"), month(dayNow, "UTC"), dayofmonth(dayNow, "UTC"), 0, 0) - ((dayofweek(dayNow, "UTC") + 5) % 7) * DAY
// the Monday (UTC midnight) of the trading week a daily bar belongs to (bar time = its 18:00 ET session start)
monOf(int t) =>
    int d = t + 6 * 3600000
    int m = timestamp("UTC", year(d, TZ), month(d, TZ), dayofmonth(d, TZ), 0, 0)
    m - ((dayofweek(m, "UTC") + 5) % 7) * DAY
// 0 = formed this week, 1 = last week, 2 = before
wkAgo(Gap g) =>
    int w = monOf(g.t0)
    w >= wkStart ? 0 : w >= wkStart - 7 * DAY ? 1 : 2
inScope(Gap g) => scM == 0 ? g.age <= LB : scM == 1 ? wkAgo(g) <= 1 : scM == 2 ? wkAgo(g) == 1 : wkAgo(g) == 0
wkTag(Gap g) => wkAgo(g) == 0 ? " · this week" : wkAgo(g) == 1 ? " · last week" : ""

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ Drawing (rebuilt on the last bar)
var array<line>  dl = array.new<line>()
var array<label> db = array.new<label>()
var array<box>   dx = array.new<box>()
// the wick CEs (premium, discount, midway) and whether the graded gap's labels have taken them
var array<float> wkP = array.new<float>(3, na)
var array<bool>  wkU = array.new<bool>(3, false)
clearAll() =>
    while dl.size() > 0
        line.delete(dl.pop())
    while db.size() > 0
        label.delete(db.pop())
    while dx.size() > 0
        box.delete(dx.pop())
lvlLab(float fr, float y) => str.tostring(fr, "0.###") + " (" + px(y) + ")"
// grade lines across a gap that is not the graded one: lvl 1 = CE · 2 = quadrants · 3 = octants
// (0 = the near edge and 1 = the far edge of the gap as it formed, prices rounded to the tick, as ICT labels them)
grades(int x1, int x2, Gap g, int lvl) =>
    int   step = lvl == 3 ? 1 : lvl == 2 ? 2 : 4
    color c = colOf(g)
    for k = 1 to 7
        if k % step == 0
            float y = math.round_to_mintick(g.bot + (g.top - g.bot) * k / 8.0)
            dl.push(line.new(x1, y, x2, y, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color.new(c, k == 4 ? 10 : 55), style = k == 4 ? line.style_dashed : line.style_dotted, width = 1))
// the graded gap, as ICT grades it on the 1-minute chart: a solid line at every eighth across the chart (edges and quadrants
// stronger), CE in its own colour and width, each line's fraction and price at the right end. On a daily chart the eighths of a
// narrow gap sit a few pixels apart, so there only the edges, CE and (from 0.75 ATR wide) the quadrants, or (from 1.5) all, are labelled
gradeF(int x1, int x2, Gap g, string nmT, string tip) =>
    float wA = (g.top - g.bot) / nz(atr, g.atr)
    int   lv = not isD or wA >= 1.5 ? 3 : wA >= 0.75 ? 2 : 1
    for k = 0 to 8
        float y  = math.round_to_mintick(g.bot + (g.top - g.bot) * k / 8.0)
        bool  ce = k == 4
        int   tr = k == 0 or k == 8 ? 25 : k % 2 == 0 ? 40 : 58
        color lc = ce ? cCE : color.new(cTx, tr)
        dl.push(line.new(x1, y, x2, y, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = lc, style = line.style_solid, width = ce ? 2 : 1))
        float fr = g.dir == 1 ? (8 - k) / 8.0 : k / 8.0
        string tx = lvlLab(fr, y) + (k == 8 and nmT != "" ? "   " + nmT : "")
        if k % 8 == 0 or ce or lv == 3 or (lv == 2 and k % 2 == 0)
            // a wick CE within a sixteenth of the gap of this line would print over its label: it joins this label instead
            for j = 0 to 2
                float w = wkP.get(j)
                if not na(w) and not wkU.get(j) and math.abs(w - y) <= (g.top - g.bot) / 16.0
                    wkU.set(j, true)
                    tx += " · wick CE " + px(w)
            db.push(label.new(x2, y, tx, xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = #00000000, textcolor = ce ? cCE : k == 8 and nmT != "" ? colOf(g) : color.new(cTx, tr - 20), size = isD ? size.tiny : size.small, tooltip = k == 8 ? tip : "", text_formatting = k == 8 and nmT != "" ? text.format_bold : text.format_none))
drawGap(Gap g, int xEnd, bool focus) =>
    color c   = colOf(g)
    bool  alt = setM == 2 and g.src == 1
    int   tr  = focus ? math.max(boxTr - 10, 0) : boxTr
    int   x1  = anchorT(g)
    dx.push(box.new(x1, g.top, xEnd, g.bot, xloc = xloc.bar_time, bgcolor = color.new(c, tr), border_color = color.new(c, 45), border_width = 1, border_style = alt ? line.style_dashed : line.style_solid))
    string nm = "D " + kindNm(g) + " · " + dayNm(g.t2) + wkTag(g) + (alt ? " · last trade" : "")
    string tip = kindNm(g) + " · " + f2((g.top - g.bot) / g.atr) + " ATR wide\n" + baseNm(g) + ", displacement candle " + dayNm(g.t2) + " (" + str.tostring(g.nc) + " candles, " + dmy(g.t1) + " – " + dmy(g.t0) + ")\n" + px(g.bot) + " – " + px(g.top) + " · CE " + px(math.round_to_mintick((g.top + g.bot) / 2.0)) + "\nwidth " + f2((g.top - g.bot) / g.atr) + " ATR · middle candle " + f2(g.disp) + " ATR, volume " + (na(g.rv) ? "—" : str.tostring(g.rv, "0.0") + "×") + (g.brk ? " · broke structure" : "") + "\n" + statusOf(g) + (alt ? "\nread with the last-trade close (SET off), so its edge may not meet the bodies on a SET chart" : "")
    // the graded gap carries its octant labels at the right end; its name goes on its first candle (daily) or on the top line
    if focus
        gradeF(x1, xEnd, g, isD ? "" : nm, tip)
        if isD
            db.push(label.new(x1, g.top, nm, xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_lower_left, color = #00000000, textcolor = c, size = size.tiny, tooltip = tip))
    else
        grades(x1, xEnd, g, gradeI == "Octants" ? 3 : gradeI == "Quadrants" ? 2 : 1)
        db.push(label.new(isD ? x1 : xEnd, role(g) == 1 ? g.top : g.bot, nm, xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = role(g) == 1 ? label.style_label_lower_left : label.style_label_upper_left, color = #00000000, textcolor = c, size = size.tiny, tooltip = tip))
// the gap's candles right of price (PO3 style): the formation candles, the gap shaded and graded, a line at the price now
drawC(float o, float h, float l, float c, int x1, int x2, int t) =>
    float bt = math.max(o, c)
    float bb = math.min(o, c)
    int   xm = int(math.round((x1 + x2) / 2))
    dx.push(box.new(x1, bt, x2, bb, xloc = xloc.bar_index, bgcolor = color.new(pCol, c >= o ? 85 : 30), border_color = pCol, border_width = 1))
    if h > bt
        dl.push(line.new(xm, bt, xm, h, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = pCol))
    if l < bb
        dl.push(line.new(xm, bb, xm, l, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = pCol))
    db.push(label.new(xm, l, str.format_time(t + 6 * 3600000, "EEE dd", TZ), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_up, color = #00000000, textcolor = cSub, size = size.tiny))
po3(Gap g) =>
    int step = pWd + pS
    int x = bar_index + pO
    int xE = x + g.nc * step
    color c = colOf(g)
    dx.push(box.new(x - 1, g.top, xE, g.bot, xloc = xloc.bar_index, bgcolor = color.new(c, 80), border_color = color.new(c, 40)))
    drawC(g.o1, g.h1, g.l1, g.c1, x, x + pWd, g.t1)
    if g.nc == 3
        drawC(g.o2, g.h2, g.l2, g.c2, x + step, x + step + pWd, g.t2)
        drawC(g.o3, g.h3, g.l3, g.c3, x + 2 * step, x + 2 * step + pWd, g.t0)
    else
        drawC(g.o2, g.h2, g.l2, g.c2, x + step, x + step + pWd, g.t0)
    dl.push(line.new(x - 1, close, xE, close, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = cTx, style = line.style_dotted, width = 1))

// the gaps on show this bar, sorted for the chart and the card
var array<Gap> shA = array.new<Gap>()    // above, nearest first
var array<Gap> shB = array.new<Gap>()    // below, nearest first
var array<Gap> shI = array.new<Gap>()    // price inside
var Gap focusG = na
int  nHid   = 0
if barstate.islast and tfOK
    clearAll()
    shA.clear()
    shB.clear()
    shI.clear()
    focusG := na
    array<Gap> all = pick()
    // FVGs before suspension blocks before imbalances, live before inverted within each, widest first: a merge keeps the first, so
    // an inversion FVG is not hidden under a suspension block or an imbalance that overlaps it
    array<Gap> cand = array.new<Gap>()
    for g in all
        int at = cand.size()
        if cand.size() > 0
            for i = 0 to cand.size() - 1
                Gap c = cand.get(i)
                int pg = g.kind * 10 + (inv(g) ? 1 : 0)
                int pc = c.kind * 10 + (inv(c) ? 1 : 0)
                if pg < pc or (pg == pc and g.top - g.bot > c.top - c.bot)
                    at := i
                    break
        cand.insert(at, g)
    array<Gap> keep = array.new<Gap>()
    for g in cand
        bool ok = inScope(g) and not (hideDef and isDef(g)) and (na(g.tX) or (showInv and g.kind == 0 and na(g.tY)))
        if ok and mergeOv and keep.size() > 0
            for k in keep
                float ov = math.min(g.top, k.top) - math.max(g.bot, k.bot)
                if role(k) == role(g) and ov >= 0.5 * math.min(g.top - g.bot, k.top - k.bot)
                    ok := false
                    break
        if ok
            keep.push(g)
        else if hideDef and isDef(g)
            nHid += 1
    // above / below / inside, against the price now
    for g in keep
        if g.bot > close
            int at = shA.size()
            if shA.size() > 0
                for i = 0 to shA.size() - 1
                    if g.bot < shA.get(i).bot
                        at := i
                        break
            shA.insert(at, g)
        else if g.top < close
            int at = shB.size()
            if shB.size() > 0
                for i = 0 to shB.size() - 1
                    if g.top > shB.get(i).top
                        at := i
                        break
            shB.insert(at, g)
        else
            shI.push(g)
    while shA.size() > nEach
        shA.pop()
    while shB.size() > nEach
        shB.pop()
    int xEnd = time + xB * timeframe.in_seconds() * 1000
    // the wick candle: the last daily swing, or yesterday. ICT grades the candle that may be turning price before the next day
    // confirms it: yesterday's lower low (higher high) than the day before is the pending swing while today has not traded past it
    bool  wYd = wickI == "Yesterday"
    bool  wPd = not wYd and wpD != 0 and (wpD == 1 ? tdL >= yL : tdH <= yH)
    bool  wUy = wYd or wPd
    float wO = wUy ? lastO : wsO
    float wH = wUy ? yH : wsH
    float wL = wUy ? yL : wsL
    float wC = wUy ? lastC : wsC
    int   wT = wUy ? lastT : wsT
    float wBt = math.max(wO, wC)
    float wBb = math.min(wO, wC)
    wkP.fill(na)
    wkU.fill(false)
    if wickI != "Off" and not na(wH) and not na(wT)
        float pw0 = math.round_to_mintick((wH + wBt) / 2.0)
        float dw0 = math.round_to_mintick((wBb + wL) / 2.0)
        if wH > wBt
            wkP.set(0, pw0)
        if wL < wBb
            wkP.set(1, dw0)
        if wH > wBt and wL < wBb
            wkP.set(2, math.round_to_mintick((pw0 + dw0) / 2.0))
    // the focus: of the gaps price is inside, an FVG (or inversion FVG) before a suspension block before an imbalance, the
    // newest first; else (Always, or a week setting) the nearest one
    for g in shI
        if na(focusG) or g.kind < focusG.kind or (g.kind == focusG.kind and g.t0 > focusG.t0)
            focusG := g
    if na(focusG) and (po3I == "Always (nearest gap)" or scM != 0)
        float dA = shA.size() > 0 ? shA.first().bot - close : na
        float dB = shB.size() > 0 ? close - shB.first().top : na
        focusG := na(dA) and na(dB) ? na : na(dB) or (not na(dA) and dA < dB) ? shA.first() : shB.first()
    for g in shA
        drawGap(g, xEnd, not na(focusG) and same(g, focusG))
    for g in shB
        drawGap(g, xEnd, not na(focusG) and same(g, focusG))
    for g in shI
        drawGap(g, xEnd, not na(focusG) and same(g, focusG))
    if not na(focusG) and (po3I == "Always (nearest gap)" or (po3I == "When price is inside a gap" and shI.size() > 0))
        po3(focusG)
    // the forming FVG is this week's: hidden with "Last week"
    if fmDir != 0 and scM != 2
        color fc = fmDir == 1 ? cBull : cBear
        dx.push(box.new(pT2, fmTop, xEnd, fmBot, xloc = xloc.bar_time, bgcolor = color.new(fc, 92), border_color = color.new(fc, 30), border_width = 1, border_style = line.style_dashed))
        dl.push(line.new(pT2, math.round_to_mintick((fmTop + fmBot) / 2.0), xEnd, math.round_to_mintick((fmTop + fmBot) / 2.0), xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color.new(fc, 40), style = line.style_dashed))
        db.push(label.new(xEnd, fmDir == 1 ? fmTop : fmBot, "D " + (fmDir == 1 ? "▲ BISI" : "▼ SIBI") + " forming · " + dayNm(lastT) + " · " + f2((fmTop - fmBot) / atr) + " ATR", xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = fmDir == 1 ? label.style_label_lower_left : label.style_label_upper_left, color = #00000000, textcolor = fc, size = size.tiny, tooltip = "Today's candle as candle 3: " + px(fmBot) + " – " + px(fmTop) + ". It stands while today's " + (fmDir == 1 ? "low stays above " + px(fmBot) : "high stays below " + px(fmTop)) + "; it joins the list at the next session's open (over a weekend, Sunday 18:00 ET)."))
    // the wick CEs of the last daily swing candle (or yesterday's), as ICT grades the wicks of the day that turned price; a CE
    // that sits on a line of the graded gap is named in that line's label, so only its line is drawn here
    if wickI != "Off"
        if not na(wH) and not na(wT)
            float bt = wBt
            float bb = wBb
            float pw = nz(wkP.get(0))
            float dw = nz(wkP.get(1))
            float mw = nz(wkP.get(2))
            string who = dayNm(wT) + (wYd ? ", yesterday" : wPd ? (wpD == 1 ? ", a pending swing low (a lower low than the day before; confirmed if today holds above " + px(yL) + ")" : ", a pending swing high (a higher high than the day before; confirmed if today holds below " + px(yH) + ")") : wsD == 1 ? ", the last daily swing low" : wsD == -1 ? ", the last daily swing high" : ", the last daily swing")
            if wH > bt
                dl.push(line.new(wT, pw, xEnd, pw, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = cWick, style = line.style_dotted))
                if not wkU.get(0)
                    db.push(label.new(xEnd, pw, "0.5 (" + px(pw) + ")", xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = #00000000, textcolor = cWick, size = size.tiny, tooltip = "Premium wick CE of " + who + ": the midpoint from its high " + px(wH) + " to its body top " + px(bt) + "."))
            if wL < bb
                dl.push(line.new(wT, dw, xEnd, dw, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = cWick, style = line.style_dotted))
                if not wkU.get(1)
                    db.push(label.new(xEnd, dw, "0.5 (" + px(dw) + ")", xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = #00000000, textcolor = cWick, size = size.tiny, tooltip = "Discount wick CE of " + who + ": the midpoint from its body bottom " + px(bb) + " to its low " + px(wL) + "."))
            if wH > bt and wL < bb
                dl.push(line.new(wT, mw, xEnd, mw, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color.new(cWick, 20), style = line.style_dashed))
                if not wkU.get(2)
                    db.push(label.new(xEnd, mw, "0.5 (" + px(mw) + ")", xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = #00000000, textcolor = color.new(cWick, 20), size = size.tiny, tooltip = "Midway between the two wick CEs of " + who + "."))

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ Alerts
var string lastAl = ""
if barstate.isrealtime and tfOK
    array<Gap> al = pick()
    for g in al
        if na(g.tX) and inScope(g)
            float ne = nearEdge(g)
            float ce = (g.top + g.bot) / 2.0
            if alIn and na(g.tT) and (g.dir == 1 ? (tdL <= ne and tdL[1] > ne) : (tdH >= ne and tdH[1] < ne))
                alert("Mangekyō · price entered the daily " + baseNm(g) + " " + px(g.bot) + "–" + px(g.top) + " (" + dayNm(g.t2) + ")", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
            if alCE and na(g.tM) and (g.dir == 1 ? (tdL <= ce and tdL[1] > ce) : (tdH >= ce and tdH[1] < ce))
                alert("Mangekyō · CE " + px(ce) + " of the daily " + baseNm(g) + " (" + dayNm(g.t2) + ") traded", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
        if newTD and inScope(g)
            if alX and not na(g.tX) and g.tX == lastT and lastAl != "x" + str.tostring(g.t0)
                lastAl := "x" + str.tostring(g.t0)
                alert("Mangekyō · the daily " + baseNm(g) + " " + px(g.bot) + "–" + px(g.top) + " closed beyond" + (g.kind == 0 and showInv ? ": now an inversion FVG" : ""), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
            if alNw and g.t0 == lastT and g.age == 0 and lastAl != "n" + str.tostring(g.t0)
                lastAl := "n" + str.tostring(g.t0)
                alert("Mangekyō · new daily " + baseNm(g) + " " + px(g.bot) + "–" + px(g.top) + " · " + f2((g.top - g.bot) / g.atr) + " ATR", alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ Card
var table tC = na
if barstate.isfirst and showCrd
    tC := table.new(posOf(crdPos), 7, 26, bgcolor = #00000000, frame_width = 0, border_color = cBd, border_width = 1, force_overlay = true)
tc(int c, int r, string s, color fg, color bg, string tip = "") =>
    tC.cell(c, r, s, text_color = fg, bgcolor = bg, text_size = crdSz, text_halign = text.align_left, tooltip = tip, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
gapRow(int r, Gap g, bool above) =>
    float w   = (g.top - g.bot) / g.atr
    float d   = na(atr) or atr <= 0 ? na : above ? (g.bot - lastC) / atr : (lastC - g.top) / atr
    bool  iv  = inv(g)
    bool  hit = (not iv and not na(g.tT)) or todayIn(g)
    float pF  = hit ? 1.0 : na(d) ? na : d <= 0 ? 1.0 : reachP(d, dLeft, above)
    float p20 = hit ? 1.0 : na(d) ? na : d <= 0 ? 1.0 : reachP(d, 20, above)
    string vm = (na(g.rv) ? "—" : str.tostring(g.rv, "0.0") + "×") + (g.brk ? " · BOS" : "")
    color c = colOf(g)
    tc(0, r, kindNm(g) + " " + dayNm(g.t2), c, cBg, baseNm(g) + " named by its displacement candle, " + dayNm(g.t2) + "; " + str.tostring(g.nc) + " candles, " + dmy(g.t1) + " – " + dmy(g.t0) + (iv ? "; closed beyond " + dmy(g.tX) + ", now an inversion FVG" : "") + (setM == 2 and g.src == 1 ? "; read with the last-trade close" : ""))
    if mob
        tc(1, r, px(g.bot) + "–" + px(g.top) + " · " + (hit ? "✓" : na(d) ? "—" : str.tostring(d, "0.0") + " ATR"), cTx, cBg)
        tc(2, r, showP ? (hit ? statusOf(g) : pc0(pF) + " by Fri") : "", cTx, cBg)
    else
        tc(1, r, px(g.bot) + "–" + px(g.top), cTx, cBg, "CE " + px(math.round_to_mintick((g.top + g.bot) / 2.0)))
        tc(2, r, f2(w) + " · " + (hit ? "✓" : na(d) ? "—" : str.tostring(d, "0.0")), cTx, cBg, "Width in ATR at formation · distance from the last close in daily ATR(14)")
        tc(3, r, statusOf(g), hit ? cTx : cSub, cBg)
        tc(4, r, showP ? (hit ? "reached" : pc0(pF) + " · " + pc0(p20)) : "", cTx, cBg)
        tc(5, r, showP ? (iv or not na(g.tT) ? "—" : pc0(pTouch(g.kind, w)) + " · " + pc0(p10(g.kind, w))) : "", cTx, cBg, iv ? "Inversion FVG: drawn, not scored (tested: no edge over the same candles without a gap)." : not na(g.tT) ? "Already touched on " + dmy(g.tT) + "; the hold odds are for the first touch day." : "If price reaches it: the touch day holds the far edge · not closed beyond within 10 days of the first touch, from the width")
        tc(6, r, vm, cSub, cBg, "The middle candle's volume against the 20 days before; BOS = the move closed beyond the last daily swing.\nTested at the same width: high-volume gaps held the touch day no more often (−2 points, z −0.8), and against the same candles without a gap their edge was +0.3 points (low volume +6.3). A break of structure added about 4 points (z 1.6; none on NQ or in 2025–26). Volume and structure are shown, not scored.")
if barstate.islast and showCrd and not na(tC)
    tC.clear(0, 0, 6, 25)
    string live = barstate.isrealtime ? "● " : "◆ "
    int nc = mob ? 2 : 6
    if not tfOK
        tc(0, 0, live + "MANGEKYŌ · use a daily or intraday chart", cTx, cHd)
    else if na(atr)
        tc(0, 0, live + "MANGEKYŌ · needs a month of daily history", cTx, cHd)
    else
        string srcT = srcI == "Front-month contract" ? "front month" : srcI == "Continuous 1!" ? "1!" : srcI == "Continuous 1!, back-adjusted" ? "1! back-adj" : "chart"
        string setT = setM == 0 ? "SET" : setM == 1 ? "last trade" : setM == 2 ? "widest" : "chart SET"
        string scT = scM == 0 ? str.tostring(LB) + "d look back" : scM == 1 ? "this + last week" : scM == 2 ? "last week" : "this week"
        tc(0, 0, live + "MANGEKYŌ   " + syminfo.ticker + "   " + srcT + " · " + setT + " · " + scT, cTx, cHd, "Daily candles from " + base + ". Bodies: " + setI + "." + (nHid > 0 ? "\n" + str.tostring(nHid) + " gap(s) from the deferred month hidden." : ""))
        tC.merge_cells(0, 0, nc, 0)
        string noneT = scM == 0 ? "in the look back" : scM == 1 ? "this or last week" : scM == 2 ? "from last week" : "this week"
        int r = 1
        if not mob
            tc(0, r, "DAILY GAP", cSub, cHd)
            tc(1, r, "RANGE", cSub, cHd)
            tc(2, r, "ATR · DIST", cSub, cHd, "Width in ATR at formation · distance from the last close")
            tc(3, r, "STATUS", cSub, cHd)
            tc(4, r, "BY FRI · 20D", cSub, cHd, "Chance the near edge trades by Friday (" + str.tostring(dLeft) + " trading day(s) left, today included) and within 20 trading days, from its distance at the last close.\nTested: gaps were reached at the same rate as any level as far away (within 20 days 84% vs 86% for the same candles without a gap), so these odds come from distance, not from the gap. Walk-forward 2014–26 (5 days): above 6→5%, 21→22%, 41→36%, 60→57%, 81→79%, 95→94%; below 6→10%, 21→22%, 40→41%, 60→61%, 80→82%, 95→95%.")
            tc(5, r, "HOLDS · 10D", cSub, cHd, "Chance the first touch day does not trade through the far edge · that it is not closed beyond within 10 trading days of the first touch, from the width.\nAgainst the same candles without a gap: the far edge held the touch day 49% vs 45% (2010–26, t 3.7; NQ, ES, RTY yes, YM no; 2010–24 and 2025–26 both). Ten days on: 29% vs 28%, no edge.")
            tc(6, r, "VOL · MS", cSub, cHd)
            r += 1
        // above: farthest first so the rows read top-down like the chart
        if shA.size() > 0
            for i = shA.size() - 1 to 0
                gapRow(r, shA.get(i), true)
                r += 1
        else
            tc(0, r, "ABOVE", cSub, cBg)
            tc(1, r, "no live gap " + noneT, cMu, cBg)
            tC.merge_cells(1, r, nc, r)
            r += 1
        tc(0, r, "— price " + px(close), cTx, cHd)
        tC.merge_cells(0, r, nc, r)
        r += 1
        if shI.size() > 0
            for i = 0 to math.min(shI.size(), 3) - 1
                gapRow(r, shI.get(i), false)
                r += 1
        if shB.size() > 0
            for g in shB
                gapRow(r, g, false)
                r += 1
        else
            tc(0, r, "BELOW", cSub, cBg)
            tc(1, r, "no live gap " + noneT, cMu, cBg)
            tC.merge_cells(1, r, nc, r)
            r += 1
        if fmDir != 0 and scM != 2
            tc(0, r, (fmDir == 1 ? "▲ BISI" : "▼ SIBI") + " forming", fmDir == 1 ? cBull : cBear, cBg, "Today's candle as candle 3 of an FVG. It counts once the day is complete and joins the list at the next session's open.")
            tc(1, r, px(fmBot) + "–" + px(fmTop) + " · " + f2((fmTop - fmBot) / atr) + " ATR · while today's " + (fmDir == 1 ? "low > " + px(fmBot) : "high < " + px(fmTop)), cTx, cBg)
            tC.merge_cells(1, r, nc, r)
            r += 1
        // the week: the nearest gap above as the premium draw, below as the discount draw
        // premium draw: the nearest resistance gap above (a SIBI, or a BISI turned inversion); discount: the nearest support below
        Gap pA = na
        Gap pB = na
        for g in shA
            if na(pA) and role(g) == -1 and (inv(g) or na(g.tT) or g.tT + 6 * 3600000 >= wkStart)
                pA := g
        for g in shB
            if na(pB) and role(g) == 1 and (inv(g) or na(g.tT) or g.tT + 6 * 3600000 >= wkStart)
                pB := g
        float dA = na(pA) ? na : (pA.bot - lastC) / atr
        float dB = na(pB) ? na : (lastC - pB.top) / atr
        string wA = na(pA) ? "premium draw —" : "premium " + kindNm(pA) + " " + px(pA.bot) + ((not inv(pA) and not na(pA.tT)) or todayIn(pA) ? " ✓" : " " + pc0(dA <= 0 ? 1.0 : reachP(dA, dLeft, true)) + " by Fri")
        string wB = na(pB) ? "discount draw —" : "discount " + kindNm(pB) + " " + px(pB.top) + ((not inv(pB) and not na(pB.tT)) or todayIn(pB) ? " ✓" : " " + pc0(dB <= 0 ? 1.0 : reachP(dB, dLeft, false)) + " by Fri")
        tc(0, r, "WEEK", cSub, cBg, "The week's range read from the daily chart, as ICT outlines it: the nearest gap above not reached before this week is the premium draw, the nearest below the discount draw, with the chance each trades by Friday (✓ = reached this week).\nTested on weekly opens 2010–26: the nearest gap above (60-day look back) was reached by the week 66–68% of the time, below 59–61%; any level as far away after similar weeks 66–68% and 60–63%. When reached, the week's extreme stopped inside the gap 27–30% of the time, as inside a same-size band without a gap (28–30%).")
        if mob
            tc(1, r, wA, cBear, cBg)
            tc(2, r, wB, cBull, cBg)
        else
            tc(1, r, wA, cBear, cBg)
            tC.merge_cells(1, r, 3, r)
            tc(4, r, wB, cBull, cBg)
            tC.merge_cells(4, r, 6, r)
        r += 1
        // today inside a gap: where the body sits against CE
        if not na(focusG) and shI.size() > 0
            Gap g = focusG
            float pos = inZ(g, close)
            int   hf  = pos <= 0 ? 0 : pos <= 0.5 ? 1 : 2
            string side = hf == 0 ? "back outside" : hf == 1 ? "near half, CE held" : "past CE"
            tc(0, r, "TODAY", cSub, cBg, "Inside the gap now. ICT: a bullish gap should keep the bodies above CE, a bearish one below.\nTested, FVGs 2010–26: when the touch day closed back outside, 44% were not closed beyond in the next 10 days; in the near half 34%; past CE 16%. The same candles without a gap: 43%, 31%, 21%. It tracks how deep price closes, at any level.")
            tc(1, r, "in " + kindNm(g) + " " + dayNm(g.t2) + " · " + side + (inv(g) ? "" : " · if today closes here, 10 more days " + pc0(pBody(g.kind, hf))), cTx, cBg)
            tC.merge_cells(1, r, nc, r)
            r += 1
